      "message": "My only concern about this is that, historically, the default/common approach to generating a profile is done *with the optimized build*. You have to deliberately use an unoptimized/unobfuscated APK to generate a profile for rewriting. I don\u0027t know the best way to detect this, but I do wonder if requiring an extra explicit step in the `dex_preopt` flow is better than assuming they\u0027ve generated their profile intentionally for rewriting. At least for now? We can still warn/fail if they don\u0027t get the right config, but that might be safer than assuming they\u0027re using the pre-rewritten profile.",
